  "worked_solution": "For our Fourier cosine series, the coefficients are given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(nx)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=-2x+5$ for $x\\in (0,\\pi ).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(-2x+5)\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(nx)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe use the integration by parts: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=-2x+5\\, & \u21d2\\,{u}^{\u2032}=-2 \\\\ {v}^{\u2032}=\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(nx)\\, & \u21d2\\,v=\\frac{1}{n}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(nx)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }(uv\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi }-{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }v{u}^{\u2032}\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }(\\frac{1}{n}[(-2x+5)\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(nx)]_{0}^{\\pi }+\\frac{2}{n}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(nx)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{n\\pi }(((-2\\pi +5)\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(n\\pi )-5\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(0))-\\frac{2}{n}[\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(nx)]_{0}^{\\pi }) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{n\\pi }(0-\\frac{2}{n}(\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(n\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(0))) \\\\  & =\\frac{4(1-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(n\\pi ))}{{n}^{2}\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, since $\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(n\\pi )=(-1)^{n},$ we have\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{4(1-(-1)^{n})}{\\pi {n}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the Fourier cosine series is\n\n$$\nf(x)\u223c(5-\\pi )+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{4(1-(-1)^{n})}{\\pi {n}^{2}}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}\u2061(nx).\n$$",
